I couldn't make the changes: all three file writes were blocked because write permission hasn't been granted in this session. Nothing in the repo has changed and I haven't run any tests.

The fix is to move `user-service.js` off the raw callback `query`/`update` calls and onto the `UserRepository` class the project is migrating to. That's the job of the project's `migrate-module` skill, and I followed its steps. If you allow edits, or run `/migrate-module src/services/user-service.js` in an interactive session, the changes below should apply as written.

**`src/services/user-service.js`**
```js
import { UserRepository } from '../repositories/user-repository.js';

const users = new UserRepository();

export function listActiveUsers() {
  return users.findActive();
}

export function findUser(id) {
  return users.findById(id);
}

export function softDeleteUser(id, when) {
  return users.softDelete(id, when);
}
```

**`tests/user-service.test.js`**: the tests `await` the functions instead of using `done` callbacks:
```js
test('listActiveUsers excludes soft-deleted users', async () => {
  const users = await listActiveUsers();
  assert.equal(users.length, 2);
  assert.ok(users.every((u) => u.deleted_at === null));
});

test('findUser returns null for an unknown id', async () => {
  const user = await findUser(999);
  assert.equal(user, null);
});
```

**`src/api/routes.js`**: the functions now return promises, so the two user routes have to turn the result back into the router's callback. Without this they would stop responding. Only these two lines change:
```js
{ method: 'GET', path: '/users', handler: (req, cb) => listActiveUsers().then((data) => cb(null, data), cb) },
{ method: 'GET', path: '/users/:id', handler: (req, cb) => findUser(Number(req.params.id)).then((data) => cb(null, data), cb) },
```

Once the edits are in, check them with `node --test tests/user-service.test.js` and then `node scripts/check-routes.js`.

